    "Figure_S3": {
      "caption": "Figure S3. Review-budget transfer and detection across all eight evaluated budgets (5 %, 10 %, 15 %, 20 %, 25 %, 30 %, 40 %, and 50 %). (A) Observed review fractions after transferring development-calibrated thresholds to the internal holdout (filled markers, solid lines; n=851) and external cohort (open markers, dashed lines; n=252); the dotted diagonal marks equality with the target budget. (B,C) Observed low-quality detection on the external (16 low-quality cases) and internal (93 low-quality cases) cohorts. Filled markers/solid lines denote transferred thresholds, and open markers/dashed lines denote cohort-specific equal-review ranking. Method A uses blue circles and method B uses orange diamonds in A–C; shapes retain method identity in grayscale. (D) External paired B-minus-A detection differences (percentage points); points are observed contrasts, and vertical bars are the archived paired Newcombe 95 % confidence intervals. Dark circles denote transferred thresholds and blue open squares denote equal review; horizontal offsets are for legibility only. The equal-review count is cohort-specific and rounded as archived; at the 20 % budget, 50 of 252 external cases are reviewed per method. Lines in A–C connect observed budget settings and do not imply additional evaluations. Source: budget_transfer/performance.csv (64 rows) and budget_transfer/paired_contrasts.csv (32 rows); all values and original intervals are unchanged.",
